---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const watchAreas = [["Japan", "Commercial", "National framework"], ["Norway", "Commercial", "IWC objection"], ["Iceland", "Commercial", "Reservation framework"], ["Greenland", "Subsistence", "Community & quota context"], ["United States", "Subsistence", "Community & legal context"], ["St. Vincent & the Grenadines", "Subsistence", "Community & quota context"]];
---
<BaseLayout title="Contemporary whaling, in context" description="Explore contemporary whaling by country, legal framework, community context, and primary source with an independent international reference.">
  <section class="hero ocean-section"><div class="container hero-layout"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">An independent reference</p><h1>Whaling is global.<br /><em>So is the context.</em></h1><p class="hero-lede">Whaling Watch maps contemporary whaling across borders, legal systems, cultures, and changing ecological questions—without reducing a complicated subject to a slogan.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/countries">Explore country context <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/sources">How we use sources <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div><div class="hero-orbit" aria-hidden="true"><div class="orbit-ring ring-one"></div><div class="orbit-ring ring-two"></div><p>OBSERVE<br />BEFORE<br />JUDGING</p><span class="bubble b1"></span><span class="bubble b2"></span><span class="bubble b3"></span></div></div><div class="surface-wave" aria-hidden="true"></div></section>
  <section class="container intro-section"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The watch</p><h2>One subject.<br /><em>Many realities.</em></h2><p>Commercial whaling, Aboriginal and subsistence whaling, national law, treaty law, population science, food systems, cultural continuity: these are not interchangeable categories. The site is built to make the distinctions visible.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container country-section"><div class="section-heading compact-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Country context</p><h2>Look wider than one flag.</h2><a class="text-link" href="/countries">View the country index →</a></div><div class="country-grid">{watchAreas.map(([country, type, context], index) => (<a class={`country-card country-card-${index + 1}`} href="/countries"><span class="card-number">0{index + 1}</span><h3>{country}</h3><p>{type}</p><small>{context}</small><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>))}</div></section>
  <section class="depth-band"><div class="container principles-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Define the practice.</h3><p>Names matter. The kind of hunt, species, location, legal basis, and stated purpose all change the meaning of a fact.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Show the rulebook.</h3><p>“Legal” and “illegal” are rarely enough. Treaties, reservations, objections, permits, quotas, and national law belong in the picture.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Keep the receipts.</h3><p>Every substantial claim should lead back to a primary, scientific, legal, or clearly identified community source.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="container closing-section"><p class="eyebrow">The long view</p><h2>Reliable information should be easier to find than a stereotype.</h2><p>Whaling Watch is being built as an accessible record: what is happening, where, why, under which rules, and how the picture changes over time.</p><a class="button button-secondary" href="/about">Read the mission <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
</BaseLayout>
